            <div xml:id="d519">

                <pb facs="0694" n="570" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg570"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/1962: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-02-21T16:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 21,
                                1921—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 5:21 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>133. Department’s no. 97, February 18. The Foreign Office did not have this
                    matter under consideration when Ambassador Geddes sailed and he left without
                    instructions on the subject. Instructions will be sent to him to take it up for
                    discussion when he reaches Washington.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
